{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And the cherubim shall be.</b> The prophets have already explained that angels in prophetic vision appear to the seers in the likeness of cherubim — with human faces and wings. In all this they signify the matter of the separate intellect, whose entire motion is upward, and this is to look toward Elohim — to intellect and to know Him, each of the separate intellects according to what is possible for it. This itself is what He now indicates by saying, וְהָיוּ הַכְּרוּבִים פֹּרְשֵׂי כְנָפַיִם לְמַעְלָה — for when the human intellect is in potentiality toward the second perfection, which it acquires by forming universals and abstracting them from matter in order to intellect and to know its Creator as far as is possible for it, this is accomplished by contemplating the wonders of His Torah, which point to the marvel of His deeds and the ways of His goodness. For indeed the essence and form of a thing are known to us through its effects, and this occurs for the human intellect when it intellects, to the extent possible for it, the existence of the Creator, blessed be He, as He said: הוֹדִיעֵנִי נָא אֶת דְּרָכֶךָ וְאֵדָעֲךָ, לְמַעַן אֶמְצָא חֵן בְּעֵינֶיךָ (Exodus 33:13). He said that the cherubim shall spread their wings upward. They have already said that the cherubim were male and female, signifying the act of producing abstracted universals — which is like the act of the male who produces — and signifying the reception of those abstracted universals — which is like the act of the female. And He said, וּפְנֵיהֶם אִישׁ אֶל אָחִיו, for the act of producing the universals and abstracting them looks toward and aims at the act of receiving the universals abstracted from matter, in which the intended perfection is acquired. And He said, אֶל הַכַּפֹּרֶת יִהְיוּ פְּנֵי הַכְּרוּבִים."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:17.217233273Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}